{**
 * c-site-header - the band across the top of every page: who this is, and the
 * way back to the start.
 *
 * Where the band sits relative to the navigation is not this component's
 * business. The shell places it into a grid area named "banner" and a theme
 * decides where that area is, which is how assets/themes/ledger.css moves the
 * navigation beside it without a line of this file changing.
 *
 * Whatever a page has to put at the far end of the band goes into the
 * siteHeaderEnd block, by {embed} - in the administration, the menu of whoever
 * is signed in. Inside the band rather than under it, so that it shares the
 * band's padding: a row drawn under the header had none, and sat on the
 * banner's bottom rule. A page that puts nothing there gets no element for it.
 *}

{define siteHeader, string $brand, string $href, string $tagline = '', ?string $testId = null}
    <div class="c-site-header l-container">
        <a class="c-site-header__brand" href="{$href}" data-testid="{$testId}">{$brand}</a>

        <p class="c-site-header__tagline" n:if="$tagline !== ''">{$tagline}</p>

        <div class="c-site-header__end" n:ifcontent>{block siteHeaderEnd}{/block}</div>
    </div>
{/define}
